julia1-cli
==========

Copyright 2026 the julia1-cli authors.

julia1-cli is a GGUF runtime for the Julia-1 decision model: a C++/ggml runtime (CLI, HTTP server, C API), a Python
package (julia1-gguf), a converter from the upstream checkpoint to GGUF, and validation tools. The names julia1-cli,
julia1-gguf and julia1 refer to the Julia-1 model, not to the Julia programming language. This is an independent
port, not affiliated with or endorsed by Supersonic Labs.

The source code in this repository is released under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE). The changes to ggml in
patches/ggml-julia1.patch are released under the MIT License, the license of ggml, so that they can be proposed
upstream (license text in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES, entry (1)).

Model and data
--------------

* Julia-1: weights, decision head, typed decision API and reference code by Supersonic Labs
  (https://huggingface.co/SupersonicLabs/Julia-1; https://supersoniclabs.ia.br/pt/julia-1/), Apache License 2.0.
  Checkpoint SHA-256 df853bf7fe424420011f3d0c47a05d7341aa9eefa7fb9f203ea4aada4ad95b72. The request encoding, the
  decision API and their validation messages in src/ and julia1_gguf/ follow its reference code. The model weights
  are not part of this repository; the GGUF conversions are published at
  https://huggingface.co/andrelucas/Julia-1-GGUF under the same license.
* Julia-1-ONNX: the ONNX export by Supersonic Labs (https://huggingface.co/SupersonicLabs/Julia-1-ONNX), Apache
  License 2.0. Its 100 parity cases are the requests of data/reference/parity.jsonl.
* mmBERT-small: the multilingual ModernBERT encoder and the tokenizer Julia-1 builds on, by Johns Hopkins University
  CLSP (https://huggingface.co/jhu-clsp/mmBERT-small; https://github.com/jhu-clsp/mmBERT; arXiv:2509.06888), MIT
  License (THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES, entry (7)).
* ModernBERT: the encoder architecture, by Answer.AI and LightOn (https://github.com/AnswerDotAI/ModernBERT;
  arXiv:2412.13663). No ModernBERT code or weights are included.
* LocalLLaMA/typed-decisions: the test set whose 2000 questions are the requests of data/reference/typed.jsonl
  (https://huggingface.co/datasets/LocalLLaMA/typed-decisions), Apache License 2.0. data/tokenizer-corpus.jsonl
  includes strings taken from these requests and from the Julia-1-ONNX parity cases. The reference logits in
  data/reference/ were computed with Julia-1's reference code in PyTorch.

Code compiled into the binaries
-------------------------------

* ggml / llama.cpp: tensor library, GGUF format and gguf-py by the ggml authors
  (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), MIT License. The build downloads release v0.5.0 and compiles its ggml
  with the changes in patches/ggml-julia1.patch; julia1-cli and the julia1_gguf_native library link that ggml
  statically, including llamafile's sgemm (Mozilla Foundation, MIT License) and ggml's YaRN RoPE code (Jeffrey
  Quesnelle and Bowen Peng, MIT License).
* nlohmann/json (https://github.com/nlohmann/json, vendored inside llama.cpp's vendor/), MIT License.
* cpp-httplib by Yuji Hirose (https://github.com/yhirose/cpp-httplib, vendored inside llama.cpp's vendor/, compiled
  into julia1-cli for its HTTP server), MIT License.

The license texts of the third-party code compiled into julia1-cli and the julia1_gguf_native library are in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.

Used for validation and benchmarks only (not distributed)
---------------------------------------------------------

* Julia-1-MLX (https://huggingface.co/zainmerchan/Julia-1-MLX) and the julia-mlx runtime
  (https://github.com/zm2231/julia-mlx), MIT License: the MLX port used as a speed and accuracy reference.
* llama.cpp PR #29363 (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/29363), the laya architecture: the target of the
  laya-layout export published with the GGUF files.
* PyTorch (https://pytorch.org/), Hugging Face transformers (https://github.com/huggingface/transformers) and
  tokenizers (https://github.com/huggingface/tokenizers), ONNX Runtime (https://onnxruntime.ai/) and MLX
  (https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx).
